isting discussion, perhaps challenge or support Agent 3's vote, bring in our own facts about other candidates, especially those not yet discussed. We have notes on A, C, D. We should bring up concerns or strengths to compare.\n\nWe need to state our current recommendation (vote). We can either support B or propose another candidate. We need to use explicit facts.\n\nLet's evaluate: Candidate A: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, understands complicated technology, but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. So strengths: decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence. Weaknesses: crew cooperation (communication difficulty, egocentric), adaptability (not willing to further education). So overall maybe okay but teamwork concerns.\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. But regarded as show-off, not open to new ideas. So strengths: technical competence, decision anticipation, leadership. Weaknesses: crew cooperation (show-off, not open), adaptability.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. But regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, stress handling maybe. Weaknesses: crew cooperation (know-it-all, hot temper), adaptability.\n\nAll have concerns. B has strong reliability, stress, technical, but uncooperative and weak memory for numbers. Memory for numbers could affect attention/accuracy. That is a concern.\n\nWe need to bring up that B's weak memory for numbers may affect attention and information accuracy, a safety-critical criterion. Also B makes nasty remarks, which is crew cooperation issue.\n\nWe could argue that B's memory issue is serious, perhaps outweighing his strengths, and that other candidates have better decision quality and technical competence, albeit with some cooperation concerns. Maybe Candidate A's quick correct decisions and calmness are strong, and his communication difficulty is a concern but maybe less severe than B's nasty remarks? Or maybe Candidate D's responsibility and problem solving outweigh his temper.\n\nWe need to decide our vote. Could we shift to Candidate A? Let's weigh: A has quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, understands technology. Those are key. Communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation, but we have no explicit evidence of nasty remarks. B's nasty remarks are explicit. So B's crew cooperation issue is more severe. Also B's weak memory for numbers is a concrete safety issue. So perhaps A is better overall.\n\nThus I might change my vote to Candidate A, citing evidence: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, technical competence, and less severe cooperation concerns (only difficulty communicating, not nasty remarks). Also note that A is not willing to further education, which may affect adaptability, but still maybe acceptable.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 3's point and bring new evidence about B's memory issue and A's strengths.\n\nThus produce public message: I am less convinced by B due to memory and nasty remarks, and propose A.\n\nLet's craft.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
